4: {'E': 2.0, 'P': 3.5, 'L': 5.0, 'E_Expl': 'The host briefly relies on their authority to regulate the debate.', 'P_Expl': 'The host uses an inviting and engaging tone, asking the senators to negotiate directly.', 'L_Expl': 'The host creates a logical progression, guiding the conversation toward a shared conclusion.', 'E_clauses': {'clause_1': 'All right, let’s go back to my question'}, 'P_clauses': {'clause_1': 'and talk to each other about it', 'clause_2': 'We can negotiate a deal right here'}, 'L_clauses': {'clause_1': 'How do you all stand on the recovery plan?', 'clause_2': 'Do you favor this plan, Senator Obama, and you, Senator McCain?', 'clause_3': 'Do you — are you in favor of this plan?'}}
0: {'E': 8.5, 'P': 4.5, 'L': 7.3, 'E_Expl': "Jim Lehrer establishes credibility by introducing himself, his role, and the Commission on Presidential Debates' sponsorship.", 'P_Expl': 'The introduction generates anticipation for the candidates and a sense of respect for the agreed-upon silence in the audience.', 'L_Expl': 'The debate format, specific subjects, and direct quotes from Eisenhower are explained in a logical manner.', 'E_clauses': {'1': 'I’m Jim Lehrer of the NewsHour on PBS', '2': 'The Commission on Presidential Debates is the sponsor of this event'}, 'P_clauses': {'1': 'The audience here in the hall has promised to remain silent, no cheers, no applause, no noise of any kind', '2': 'as we welcome Senators Obama and McCain. (APPLAUSE)'}, 'L_clauses': {'1': 'Tonight’s will primarily be about foreign policy and national security, which, by definition, includes the global financial crisis', '2': 'Direct exchanges between the candidates and moderator follow-ups are permitted after each candidate has two minutes to answer the lead question in an order determined by a coin toss', '3': 'The specific subjects and questions were chosen by me. They have not been shared or cleared with anyone', '4': 'Quote, “We must achieve both security and solvency. In fact, the foundation of military strength is economic strength,” end quote'}}
3: {'E': 7.5, 'P': 8.4, 'L': 6.7, 'E_Expl': 'The speaker establishes credibility by expressing concern for Senator Kennedy, thanking the university, and showing experience with the crisis.', 'P_Expl': 'The speaker evokes emotions by mentioning personal difficulties, the struggles of everyday Americans, and the need to overcome the crisis.', 'L_Expl': 'The speaker uses logical arguments to discuss the bipartisan nature of the solution, the features of the proposed package, and the need to create jobs and eliminate dependence on foreign oil.', 'E_clauses': {'1': 'Senator Kennedy is in the hospital.', '2': 'I also want to thank the University of Mississippi for hosting us tonight.', '3': 'certainly in our time, and I’ve been around a little while.'}, 'P_clauses': {'1': 'I’ve been not feeling too great about a lot of things lately.', '2': 'So have a lot of Americans who are facing challenges.', '3': 'we’re talking about failures on Main Street, and people who will lose their jobs, and their credits, and their homes, if we don’t fix the greatest fiscal crisis'}, 'L_clauses': {'1': 'we are seeing, for the first time in a long time, Republicans and Democrats together, sitting down, trying to work out a solution to this fiscal crisis that we’re in.', '2': 'This package has transparency in it.', '3': 'we’ve got to create jobs. And one of the areas, of course, is to eliminate our dependence on foreign oil.'}}
1: {'E': 7.5, 'P': 8.2, 'L': 8.8, 'E_Expl': 'Credibility established through acknowledging the host and expressing the importance of the debate.', 'P_Expl': 'Appeals to the emotions of the audience by highlighting the challenges faced by everyday Americans.', 'L_Expl': 'Provides logical steps that aim to address the financial crisis and its impact on homeowners.', 'E_clauses': {'1': 'Well, thank you very much, Jim, and thanks to the commission and the University of Mississippi, Ole Miss, for hosting us tonight.'}, 'P_clauses': {'1': 'And although we’ve heard a lot about Wall Street, those of you on Main Street I think have been struggling for a while, and you recognize that this could have an impact on all sectors of the economy.', '2': 'And you’re wondering, how’s it going to affect me? How’s it going to affect my job? How’s it going to affect my house? How’s it going to affect my retirement savings or my ability to send my children to college?'}, 'L_clauses': {'1': 'So we have to move swiftly, and we have to move wisely.', '2': 'And I’ve put forward a series of proposals that make sure that we protect taxpayers as we engage in this important rescue effort.', '3': 'Number one, we’ve got to make sure that we’ve got oversight over this whole process; $700 billion, potentially, is a lot of money.', '4': 'Number two, we’ve got to make sure that taxpayers, when they are putting their money at risk, have the possibility of getting that money back and gains, if the market — and when the market returns.', '5': 'Number three, we’ve got to make sure that none of that money is going to pad CEO bank accounts or to promote golden parachutes.', '6': 'And, number four, we’ve got to make sure that we’re helping homeowners, because the root problem here has to do with the foreclosures that are taking place all across the country.'}}
